{{!
    @template mod_examcheck/conflict_toast

    Body of the "already checked" warning toast shown by the scanner: the conflict
    message plus a link back to the roster focused on the matched student. Rendered to
    HTML and passed as the message to core/toast (whose template outputs it unescaped),
    so all dynamic values are escaped here.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * message string The localised "already checked" sentence.
    * rosterlink string URL to the roster focused on the matched student.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "message": "Already checked: Jane Doe (EX4) was marked by Admin User, 4 seconds ago.",
        "rosterlink": "https://example.org/mod/examcheck/view.php?id=2&userid=6"
    }
}}
<div>{{ message }}</div>
<div class="mt-1">
    <a href="{{ rosterlink }}">{{#str}} view_in_roster, mod_examcheck {{/str}}</a>
</div>
